# Canonical Turtle for the protocol-derived encoding of:
#   Mohammed Azeez Khan et al. (2026). Active Learning Strategies for Efficient Machine-Learned Interatomic Potentials Across Diverse Material Systems.
#   arXiv (Cornell University). doi:10.48550/arxiv.2601.06916  arXiv:2601.06916v2
#
# Version read: arxiv-preprint arXiv:2601.06916v2 (sha256 64301c14eb822f4a...);
#   the DOI above is cited, numbers are those of the version read.
# Corpus rank 652 (Training/reliability). Method identity follows
#   artifacts/kg/METHODS.md (registry: artifacts/kg/methods-registry.csv).
# Generated by artifacts/scripts/encode_paper.py from artifacts/kg/encoding/specs/khan2026.yaml.
#
# Encoding scope: none beyond the study record. Despite its title, the
# paper trains ensembles of feed-forward networks that regress formation
# energy per atom from 17 compositional and property descriptors of
# Materials Project and OQMD structures (500-600 per system) and compares
# random, uncertainty, diversity and hybrid query strategies. The models
# take no atomic positions and give no forces, so they are not
# interatomic potentials and are not encoded as runs.

